## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curlnoise3d.html
- Summary (EN): Generates a 3D divergence-free noise field built as a fractal curl of Perlin noise. Outputs a vector field as an RGB layer or a Vector VDB, sampled at world coordinates.
- Résumé (FR) : Produit un champ vectoriel 3D sans divergence en coordonnées monde, construit comme rotationnel fractal de bruit de Perlin.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref (required): representative layer setting output size and metadata", "pos (optional): layer or VDB giving the position at each pixel", "octaves (optional): multiplier applied to Max Octaves", "roughness (optional): multiplier applied to Roughness"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Amplitude: scales the noise before Center", "Center: offsets the output range", "Element Size: world-space size of the basic element; Element Scale per axis with Per-Component Controls", "Offset: shifts the noise function in world coordinates", "Max Octaves: number of stacked noise layers", "Lacunarity: scale change per octave", "Roughness: amplitude change per octave", "Octave Offset: positional offset per octave"]

- Caveats: ["Amplitude and Center can push values outside the expected range; add a Clamp COP to enforce it.", "Unlike Curl Noise, samples at world coordinates rather than image coordinates."]

